      "snippets": [
        {
          "source_line": 22,
          "tex": "\\noindent\nIn this chapter we use the material from the preceding sections to\ngive criteria under which a presheaf of sets on the category of schemes\nis an algebraic space. Some of this material comes from the work\nof Artin, see \\cite{ArtinI}, \\cite{ArtinII},\n\\cite{Artin-Theorem-Representability},\n\\cite{Artin-Construction-Techniques},\n\\cite{Artin-Algebraic-Spaces},\n\\cite{Artin-Algebraic-Approximation},\n\\cite{Artin-Implicit-Function},\nand \\cite{ArtinVersal}.\nHowever, our method will be to use as much as possible arguments\nsimilar to those of the paper by Keel and Mori, see\n\\cite{K-M}."
        }
      ],
      "stage_a_readiness": "no_active_candidates"
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "kind": "context_only",
      "source_line": 37,
      "snippets": [
        {
          "source_line": 46,
          "tex": "Let $S$ be a scheme and let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$.\nIn this chapter and the following we will write $X \\times_S X$\nfor the product of $X$ with itself (in the category of algebraic\nspaces over $S$), instead of $X \\times X$."
        }
      ],
      "stage_a_readiness": "no_active_candidates"
